  "notes": "Atlanta’s live-instrument melodic bench — the \"retro-future\" school. Two documented parameters set it apart from everything else in this lane: **vintage-keyboard harmony pushes it out of one-chord vamps**, and **the bass is a live electric bass rather than an 808 on most records**. Live guitar sits alongside it, and the sequencing is Ableton with sounds pulled from Logic and Reason. ⚠ `medium`: DAW, sound sources, specific vintage keyboards, the live-versus-programmed split and the personnel are all documented — the research rates it high-medium. ⚠ A progression family authored `Imaj7`, which `Numeral::parse` cannot read — it knows i, VI, bII and vii° and takes the seventh from `chords.extensions`, not from the numeral. An unreadable numeral makes the generator skip the slot, so that whole family produced NO CHORDS AT ALL, and chords.rs caught it only when a seed happened to pick it. Now `I`; the major-7th colour is carried by the extensions block, where it was always meant to be.",
